THOUGHT: The new NullAway error arises because `getConfigurationProperty` accepts a nullable `ConfigurationPropertyName name` and then passes it directly to `ConfigurationProperty.of`, whose `name` parameter is now non-null. The logic already treats a null `name` as valid only for computing a prefixed name; but if `name` is null, we shouldn’t construct a `ConfigurationProperty` with a null name. A simple, safe fix is to return `null` early when `name` is null, avoiding the invalid call. I’ll add this null check, then re-run the compile to ensure the total NullAway error count drops from 84 to 83.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/spring-boot && sed -i 's/@Override
		public ConfigurationProperty getConfigurationProperty(@Nullable ConfigurationPropertyName name) {
-			ConfigurationProperty configurationProperty = this.source.getConfigurationProperty(getPrefixedName(name));
+			if (name == null) {
+				return null;
+			}
+			ConfigurationProperty configurationProperty = this.source.getConfigurationProperty(getPrefixedName(name));/' spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/context/properties/source/PrefixedConfigurationPropertySource.java && nl -ba spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/context/properties/source/PrefixedConfigurationPropertySource.java | sed -n '40,70p' && ./gradlew :spring-boot-project:spring-boot:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 || true && (grep -n "PrefixedConfigurationPropertySource.java" new_build_output.log || echo "No PrefixedConfigurationPropertySource.java errors") && grep " errors" new_build_output.log | tail -n 1
```

